.TH OSDCTL 1 "@DATE@" "Objectspace @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
osdctl \- talk to osdd, the Objectspace object service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B osdctl
.I command
.RI [ arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B osdctl
sends one request to
.BR osdd ,
the per-user service that keeps Objectspace's objects (files, folders, shadows,
programs, settings objects), and prints its answer as JSON.
osdd listens on
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/objectspace.sock
and is started with the graphical session.
.PP
A
.I TARGET
is a path, or a central object's
.BI vobj: ID\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ping
osdd's version, protocol and identity.
.TP
.BR stats " | " flush " | " sync " | " scan " | " shutdown " | " setup
Counters; write pending state; sync portable volumes; rescan watched
folders; stop osdd; make the settings objects.
.TP
.BI resolve " TARGET"
The object for a path: its ID, class and title.
.TP
.BI call " " \fR[\fB\-\-expect\fI " N" \fR]\fI " TARGET METHOD " \fR[\fIARG\fR...]
Call a method of the object (for example
.BR osdSetTitle ).
.TP
.BI describe " CLASS"
A class's methods and parent.
.TP
.BI shadow " TARGET FOLDER"
Make a shadow of TARGET in FOLDER.
.TP
.BI create " FOLDER CLASS TITLE " \fR[\fICOMMAND\fR]
Make an object of CLASS in FOLDER (a program with COMMAND).
.TP
.BI list " FOLDER " \fR[\fIOFFSET\fR " " [\fICOUNT\fR " " [\fBdetails\fR]]]
A page of FOLDER's contents.
.TP
.BI find " FOLDER PATTERN " \fR[\fBsub\fR] " " [\fBany\fR|\fBfolder\fR|\fBfile\fR|\fBprogram\fR] " " [\fILIMIT\fR]
Search FOLDER (and its subfolders with
.BR sub ).
.TP
.BI select " FOLDER " "all \fR[\fIEXCEPT\fR...] | " "select " "FOLDER ITEM\fR..."
Make a selection, for
.BR move " and " copy .
.TP
.BI move\fR|\fBcopy " SELECTION DEST"
Start a job; its ID is printed.
.TP
.BI job " ID" "\fR | \fBjobs\fR | \fBjob_cancel\fR|\fBjob_pause\fR|\fBjob_resume " ID
Follow and control jobs;
.BI job_decide " ID " skip\fR|\fBrename " " \fR[\fBall\fR]
answers a job's question.
.TP
.BI menu " TARGET" "\fR | \fBmenu_select " "TARGET ITEM" "\fR | \fBsettings " TARGET
The object's menu, one of its items, its settings pages.
.TP
.BI settings_set " TARGET KEY" = VALUE ...
Change settings, as its notebook does.
.TP
.BR watch " [" folder
.IR PATH "]... [" object
.IR TARGET "]... [" jobs ]
Print events as they come.
.TP
.BI open " TARGET " \fR[\fBconfirm\fR] "\fR | \fBfrom_template " "TEMPLATE FOLDER TITLE" "\fR | \fBrename " "TARGET NAME"
Open an object; make one from a template; rename one.
.TP
.BI layout " FOLDER" "\fR | \fBarrange " FOLDER "\fR | \fBplace " "FOLDER TARGET X Y " \fR[\fITARGET X Y\fR]...
Icon positions: read them, arrange them, set them.
.TP
.BI vmove " vobj:ID FOLDER " \fR[\fBcopy\fR]
Move (or copy) a central object to another folder.
.TP
.BR restore-defaults " [" \fIDESKTOP\fR ]
Put back the desktop's default objects (System, Programs, Trash Can and
what System holds) where they were moved, trashed or deleted; as the
Restore Desktop object does.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OSD_SOCKET
osdd's socket, instead of
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/objectspace.sock .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/objectspace
Objects and the database.
.TP
.I ~/.config/objectspace
Settings and the first start's marker.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR osd-shell (1),
.BR osd-session (1)
